(https://github.com/google-research/paper-orchestra, commit d9bae99),
Copyright 2026 Google LLC, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(see LICENSE-APACHE-2.0).

Modifications (2026, PaperOrchestra skill pack): the Gemini client is replaced
by a call layer (llm.py) that writes each model input to a file for a host
coding agent to answer; pipeline branches are named so a run can be resumed;
optional dependencies have fallbacks; diagrams are drawn as matplotlib code
because the host has no image model. Each modified file states its changes in
its header. The full line-by-line diff is in docs/official-port.diff.

"PaperOrchestra" is the name of the method by Yiwen Song, Yale Song, Tomas
Pfister and Jinsung Yoon (Google Cloud AI Research). This skill pack is an
independent adaptation and is not an official Google product.
